        "original_id": "3163cb55-cc75-5e4e-bfb3-8beeb68e6498",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lysichiton, Ageratum, Orontioideae, Orontium, Symplocarpus, Arisaema candidissimum\n- Taxonomy: Araceae, Asteraceae, Eupatorieae, genera, subfamily, species\n- Places: North America, Asia, eastern North America, western China, Tibet, Sichuan, Yunnan\n\nFacts:\n- Lysichiton is a genus in the family Araceae.\n- Ageratum is a genus of 40 to 60 tropical and warm temperate flowering annuals and perennials in the family Asteraceae and tribe Eupatorieae.\n- In the USA, Ageratum is called whiteweed.\n- Orontioideae consists of three genera: Lysichiton, Orontium, and Symplocarpus.\n- Lysichiton includes one to two species of skunk cabbage from North America and Asia.\n- Orontium includes one living species from eastern North America and two extinct species known from fossils.\n- Symplocarpus includes several species of skunk cabbage from North America and Asia.\n- Arisaema candidissimum is a species of flowering plant in the arum family, Araceae.\n- Arisaema candidissimum originates in western China, including Tibet, Sichuan, and Yunnan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
